 "text": "**Starling Bank is the strongest all-round choice for most people switching to an app-based bank in the UK.**\n\nMoneySavingExpert (updated November 2026) ranks it as the top all-rounder among app-based current accounts. It offers a free personal account with no monthly fee, competitive arranged overdraft rates (typically 15%, 25% or 35% EAR), 24/7 UK-based support, solid budgeting tools (Spaces, spending insights, bills tools, round-ups), and no Starling fees on card spending or ATM withdrawals abroad. It supports cash deposits (free up to £1,000 a year at the Post Office, then a fee) and cheque imaging, participates in the Current Account Switch Service, and eligible deposits are FSCS-protected (currently up to £120,000 per person per authorised firm).\n\n### How the main options compare\n| Priority | Best fit | Key points |\n|----------|----------|------------|\n| Everyday main account | **Starling** | Free, strong overseas use (no bank fees, no monthly ATM cap from Starling), lower overdraft rates than many rivals, good app tools, cash/cheque options |\n| Hands-on budgeting | **Monzo** | Excellent Pots, categorisation, salary sorting and notifications; free tier is capable but overseas ATM withdrawals have limits and some extras sit on paid plans |\n| Cashback + savings rates | **Chase UK** | Often strong linked saver rates (with bonuses) and cashback on eligible spending (conditions and caps apply, e.g. minimum activity/balance rules); no overdraft; limited cash deposits |\n| Interest on the balance itself | **Kroo** or **Zopa** | Kroo pays interest on current-account balances; Zopa offers cashback options or interest. Check features carefully (e.g. Kroo is not on the full switch service) |\n| Frequent travel / multi-currency | **Revolut** | Flexible currencies and FX tools; free tier has fair-use limits on fee-free exchange and ATMs. It has been moving UK customers onto full bank accounts with FSCS protection—confirm your account type |\n\n### Practical advice before switching\n- **You don’t have to fully switch.** Many people keep a high-street account and use an app bank alongside it (or the reverse).\n- Use the **Current Account Switch Service** if you want Direct Debits, standing orders and salary payments moved automatically. It is free and guaranteed to complete in seven working days for participating banks (Starling, Monzo and Chase participate; some smaller providers do not).\n- Rates, cashback rules, bonuses and limits change often. Check the bank’s own site for the latest figures, eligibility and any fair-use policies before opening or moving money.\n- Confirm **FSCS protection** applies to the specific account you open. Fully licensed UK banks (Starling, Monzo, Chase, Kroo, Zopa and others) protect eligible deposits; pure e-money providers do not in the same way.\n- Think about practical needs: frequent cash deposits, overdrafts, joint accounts, or branch access. Pure app banks have no branches, and support is via chat/phone.\n\nFor a straightforward free everyday account with good travel features and customer support, start with **Starling**. If budgeting tools or cashback matter more, compare Monzo or Chase side-by-side with your actual spending.",
